WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.677
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:14.253
Unit twelve: Consumer Habits. Today you will talk about marketing with the passive voice.

4
00:00:14.553 --> 00:00:17.228
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:21.527
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.383 --> 00:00:23.512
Consumerism.

7
00:00:24.517 --> 00:00:27.840
Consumerism means the idea that buying more things is good.

8
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.833
Consumerism creates a lot of waste.

9
00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:34.278
Your turn. Say: Consumerism.

10
00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.227
Consumerism.

11
00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:40.077
Brand loyalty.

12
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:44.244
Brand loyalty means always buying from the same company.

13
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.175
My dad has strong brand loyalty.

14
00:00:47.783 --> 00:00:50.482
Your turn. Say: Brand loyalty.

15
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.776
Brand loyalty.

16
00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:56.680
Advertising.

17
00:00:57.683 --> 00:01:00.995
Advertising means telling people about products to sell them.

18
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:03.722
Advertising is everywhere online.

19
00:01:04.317 --> 00:01:06.865
Your turn. Say: Advertising.

20
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.875
Advertising.

21
00:01:11.617 --> 00:01:12.838
Impulse buying.

22
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:17.034
Impulse buying means buying things suddenly without planning.

23
00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:19.708
Impulse buying wastes money.

24
00:01:20.317 --> 00:01:23.004
Your turn. Say: Impulse buying.

25
00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:27.100
Impulse buying.

26
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.466
Sustainable choice.

27
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:34.121
Sustainable choice means a choice that is better for the planet.

28
00:01:34.717 --> 00:01:37.761
A reusable bottle is a sustainable choice.

29
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:41.629
Your turn. Say: Sustainable choice.

30
00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:46.153
Sustainable choice.

31
00:01:46.917 --> 00:01:48.104
Product review.

32
00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:52.196
Product review means an opinion about something you can buy.

33
00:01:52.783 --> 00:01:55.003
I read product reviews before I buy.

34
00:01:55.617 --> 00:01:58.617
Your turn. Say: Product review.

35
00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:02.781
Product review.

36
00:02:03.517 --> 00:02:04.831
Ethical shopping.

37
00:02:05.817 --> 00:02:10.161
Ethical shopping means buying from companies that treat people and nature fairly.

38
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.226
Ethical shopping supports fair workers.

39
00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:16.736
Your turn. Say: Ethical shopping.

40
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.868
Ethical shopping.

41
00:02:21.617 --> 00:02:22.571
Marketing.

42
00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:26.883
Marketing means ways companies promote and sell products.

43
00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:29.692
Clever marketing targets teenagers.

44
00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.796
Your turn. Say: Marketing.

45
00:02:35.633 --> 00:02:36.553
Marketing.

46
00:02:37.317 --> 00:02:38.271
Trend-driven.

47
00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:42.200
Trend-driven means influenced by what is popular now.

48
00:02:42.817 --> 00:02:45.199
Trend-driven shopping changes every month.

49
00:02:45.783 --> 00:02:48.540
Your turn. Say: Trend-driven.

50
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.459
Trend-driven.

51
00:02:53.217 --> 00:02:54.125
Value.

52
00:02:55.117 --> 00:02:58.788
Value means how useful or important something is for its price.

53
00:02:59.383 --> 00:03:00.930
This bag is good value.

54
00:03:01.517 --> 00:03:03.821
Your turn. Say: Value.

55
00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:07.784
Value.

56
00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.132
Quality over quantity.

57
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:14.428
Quality over quantity means having fewer but better things.

58
00:03:15.017 --> 00:03:17.086
I choose quality over quantity.

59
00:03:17.683 --> 00:03:21.230
Your turn. Say: Quality over quantity.

60
00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.590
Quality over quantity.

61
00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:27.409
Minimalism.

62
00:03:28.417 --> 00:03:31.333
Minimalism means living simply with fewer things.

63
00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.100
Minimalism helps me save money.

64
00:03:34.717 --> 00:03:37.241
Your turn. Say: Minimalism.

65
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.089
Minimalism.

66
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.562
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:46.417 --> 00:03:48.706
Visal, do ads influence what you buy?

68
00:03:49.817 --> 00:03:55.255
Yes. Products are often advertised by influencers I follow.

69
00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.013
Do you buy on impulse?

70
00:03:59.117 --> 00:04:03.963
Sometimes. Many of my choices are influenced by marketing.

71
00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.481
How can you change that?

72
00:04:07.583 --> 00:04:12.172
I read product reviews first, and I choose quality over quantity.

73
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:14.938
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:15.783 --> 00:04:18.201
Grammar focus: Passive voice.

75
00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:19.757
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.670
Products are often advertised heavily.

77
00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:25.641
Choices are influenced by marketing.

78
00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:28.666
This phone is made in Vietnam.

79
00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.935
Use the passive when the action is more important than who does it.

80
00:04:33.683 --> 00:04:37.311
Be careful! Don't say: Products are advertise heavily.

81
00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:41.858
Say: Products are advertised heavily.

82
00:04:42.158 --> 00:04:44.193
The passive needs the past participle.

83
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.385
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.549
Smart Shopping.

85
00:04:49.849 --> 00:04:52.580
Advertising often encourages impulse buying.

86
00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:56.414
Many products are marketed directly to teenagers.

87
00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.396
Our choices are influenced by trend-driven marketing and brand loyalty.

88
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.386
I try ethical shopping and read each product review.

89
00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:10.780
Choosing quality over quantity reflects sustainable, minimalist values.

90
00:05:11.867 --> 00:05:15.799
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.766
Products blank advertised online.

92
00:05:19.066 --> 00:05:21.581
A, are. B, is. C, be.

93
00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:27.028
The answer is A: are.

94
00:05:28.183 --> 00:05:30.787
Buying things suddenly without planning is blank.

95
00:05:31.087 --> 00:05:35.193
A, impulse buying. B, minimalism. C, brand loyalty.

96
00:05:38.733 --> 00:05:40.826
The answer is A: impulse buying.

97
00:05:41.983 --> 00:05:44.262
Living simply with fewer things is blank.

98
00:05:44.562 --> 00:05:48.424
A, minimalism. B, consumerism. C, marketing.

99
00:05:51.967 --> 00:05:54.036
The answer is A: minimalism.

100
00:05:55.233 --> 00:05:58.501
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:02.383
How do advertisements influence your shopping habits?

102
00:06:11.183 --> 00:06:12.637
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:12.937 --> 00:06:22.091
Many of my choices are influenced by ads on social media. Now I wait one day before buying, and I read reviews first.

104
00:06:22.391 --> 00:06:24.019
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:28.788
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and passive voice.

106
00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:33.493
Today's value is saving wisely. Save a little money and spend it carefully.

107
00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:36.759
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:37.059 --> 00:06:39.607
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

